/**
\dir src
\brief FORCES library sources.
\details Fortran modules provide numerical methods, spatial and temporal data
handling, file I/O, and application utilities. The C backends support operating
system operations in mo_os and error-message copying in mo_netcdf_wrapper.
Browse the library by purpose through \ref f_core, \ref f_spatial, \ref f_time,
\ref f_io, \ref f_statistics, and \ref f_optimization.
*/

/**
\defgroup f_core Core utilities and data structures
\brief Numeric kinds, constants, arrays, strings, graphs, and application support.
\details Common building blocks include array operations and sorting, linked
lists and directed acyclic graphs, sentinel values, command-line parsing,
logging, timing, and library version information.
\par Examples
- \ref 02_dag/01_dag_sort.f90 constructs and sorts a directed acyclic graph.
- \ref 02_dag/02_branching.f90 traverses a branching graph from leaves or roots.
- \ref 03_log/01_logging_cli.F90 configures logging from command-line options.
- \ref 04_utils/01_prefix_sum.f90 compares cumulative sums and prefix sums.
*/

/**
\defgroup f_spatial Spatial data and regridding
\brief Structured grids, point sets, polygons, spatial indexing, and mapping.
\details Grid and point representations support packing and masking, geometric
operations, nearest-neighbor searches, spatial scaling, and comparison of
spatial patterns. Dataset readers and writers are collected in \ref f_io.
\par Examples
- \ref 01_grids/01_regridding.f90 regrids a DEM read from an ASCII file.
- \ref 01_grids/03_nc_regridder.f90 regrids data read from NetCDF.
- \ref 01_grids/04_nc_nearest.f90 demonstrates nearest-neighbor grid mapping.
- \ref 01_grids/05_grid_fill_border.f90 fills missing DEM cells from its border.
- \ref 05_points/02_points_nearest.f90 maps the nearest gauge onto a grid.
*/

/**
\defgroup f_time Dates and time series
\brief Calendars, time axes, temporal aggregation, resampling, and filtering.
\details Date and time types and Julian conversions support time-axis handling.
Temporal aggregation and resampling operate on time-series values, while the
Eckhardt filter separates baseflow from discharge series. Dataset I/O belongs to
\ref f_io; general statistical analysis belongs to \ref f_statistics.
\par Example
\ref 05_points/04_points_timeseries_resample.f90 resamples daily interval-mean
discharge to hourly values and writes a point time-series dataset.
*/

/**
\defgroup f_io File I/O and operating system support
\brief Text, namelist, and NetCDF I/O, file patterns, paths, and directories.
\details Dataset abstractions read and write gridded and point data, including
time series. Shared NetCDF helpers and the C interoperability backends support
these interfaces. Path utilities and glob matching locate files and directories.
\par Examples
- \ref 01_grids/02_nc_output.f90 writes gridded variables to NetCDF.
- \ref 05_points/01_points_io.f90 writes discharge at gauge locations.
- \ref 05_points/03_points_timeseries_io.f90 writes station IDs and time series.
*/

/**
\defgroup f_statistics Statistics and numerical methods
\brief Descriptive statistics, transformations, regression, errors, and integration.
\details Statistical routines provide moments, percentiles, histograms,
autocorrelation, normalization, outlier detection, and random number generation.
Numerical tools cover polynomial operations and integration, linear and kernel
regression, density estimation, and error measures. Parameter optimization and
posterior sampling are collected in \ref f_optimization.
*/

/**
\defgroup f_optimization Optimization and sampling
\brief Parameter search algorithms, objective interfaces, and posterior sampling.
\details Simulated annealing, Dynamically Dimensioned Search, Nelder-Mead, and
Shuffled Complex Evolution minimize objective functions. Markov chain Monte
Carlo samples posterior distributions. Shared objective types, evaluation
helpers, and benchmark cost and likelihood functions support these algorithms.
*/

/**
\dir include
\brief Preprocessor headers for FORCES applications.
\details The logging.h header supplies the logging macros used with mo_logging.
*/

/**
\dir doc
\brief FORCES documentation and presentation assets.
\details Doxygen configuration, directory descriptions, HTML customizations,
PDF styles, figures, release history, and Read the Docs build support.
*/

/**
\dir examples
\brief Standalone programs demonstrating the FORCES library.
\details Examples cover structured grids, directed acyclic graphs, logging,
array utilities, and point time series. Build and run a program from the
repository root, for example:
\code{.sh}
cmake -S . -B build_example -DFORCES_EXE=examples/04_utils/01_prefix_sum.f90
cmake --build build_example --parallel 4
./build_example/main
\endcode
Use the repository root as the working directory for examples that read fixtures
from \c src/pf_tests/files. NetCDF examples require FORCES_WITH_NETCDF=ON.
*/

/**
\dir examples/01_grids
\brief Structured grid regridding, NetCDF output, and border filling.
\details
- \ref 01_grids/01_regridding.f90 demonstrates DEM regridding from an ASCII input.
- \ref 01_grids/02_nc_output.f90 writes grid variables to NetCDF.
- \ref 01_grids/03_nc_regridder.f90 regrids NetCDF data between structured grids.
- \ref 01_grids/04_nc_nearest.f90 demonstrates nearest-neighbor grid mapping.
- \ref 01_grids/05_grid_fill_border.f90 writes a DEM border mask and fills missing
  cells using nearest source border cells.
*/

/**
\dir examples/02_dag
\brief Directed acyclic graph construction and ordering.
\details
- \ref 02_dag/01_dag_sort.f90 demonstrates topological and level-based sorting.
- \ref 02_dag/02_branching.f90 builds a branching graph from downstream links
  and traverses its levels from either roots or leaves.
*/

/**
\dir examples/03_log
\brief Command-line configuration of application logging.
\details \ref 03_log/01_logging_cli.F90 combines mo_cli with the logging.h macros
and mo_logging. It demonstrates log-level options and redirection to a log file.
The uppercase \c .F90 extension enables preprocessing of the logging macros.
*/

/**
\dir examples/04_utils
\brief Array utility examples.
\details \ref 04_utils/01_prefix_sum.f90 compares mo_utils prefix sums and
cumulative sums, including shifted output and a starting offset. With OpenMP
enabled, it also reports timings for larger arrays.
*/

/**
\dir examples/05_points
\brief Point data, nearest-neighbor mapping, and time-series NetCDF I/O.
\details
- \ref 05_points/01_points_io.f90 writes synthetic discharge on gauge locations.
- \ref 05_points/02_points_nearest.f90 maps the nearest gauge onto a regular grid.
- \ref 05_points/03_points_timeseries_io.f90 writes station IDs and discharge
  using a point time-series output dataset.
- \ref 05_points/04_points_timeseries_resample.f90 resamples daily interval means
  to hourly values and writes the resulting point time series.
These examples read gauge coordinates from \c src/pf_tests/files/scc_gauges.nc
and require NetCDF support.
*/
